# Build context for the Compose stack in `infra/compose/`.
#
# The context is the repository root, so a `COPY apps/api/src/api` needs the
# whole tree available to Docker before it discards anything. Without this file
# every build uploads the virtualenv, five caches, and the training data -- on a
# 1-core box with 48 GB of disk that is minutes of upload per build and
# gigabytes of context nobody reads.
#
# Anything excluded here that a Dockerfile then tries to COPY is a build
# failure, not a silent omission, so this list is safe to keep aggressive.
#
# **Leading slashes are load-bearing.** A pattern without one matches at any
# depth, so a bare `model/` would also exclude `ml/src/ml/model/` -- the torch
# network and checkpoint code the inference image imports. The build would fail
# with an import error naming a package that is sitting right there on disk.
# `.gitignore` carries a comment about this same trap for `/model/`; the
# directory-anchored patterns below are all deliberate and all start with `/`.

# --- Version control and editor noise ---
/.git/
/.gitignore
/.gitattributes
/.github/

# --- Python environments and tool caches ---
# `.venv/` alone is several hundred megabytes, and on a Windows checkout it is
# Windows wheels that could not run in a Linux image anyway.
# These two are matched at any depth on purpose: `__pycache__` appears inside
# every source package.
/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
/.mypy_cache/
/.ruff_cache/
/.pytest_cache/
/.import_linter_cache/

# --- Data and model artefacts ---
# `data/training/signals.npy` is 58 MB on its own. These are mounted into the
# inference container at runtime rather than baked into an image, so they are
# never part of a build.
/data/
/colab_report/
/model/
*.pt
*.ckpt
*.pth

# --- Notebooks ---
# The Colab training notebook is orchestration, not something the stack runs.
/ml/notebooks/

# --- Local scratch and planning material ---
/.local/
/spec_driven_development/
/README.full.md

# --- Node ---
# The frontend, in full. Neither image copies anything from `apps/web` -- the
# Vercel build does that, somewhere else entirely -- so the whole directory is
# build context that would be uploaded and then discarded. `node_modules/`
# alone is hundreds of megabytes.
#
# Matched at any depth as well, because `apps/web/node_modules` is the one that
# actually exists.
node_modules/
/apps/web/

# --- Test and dev configuration ---
# None of it is imported by any container: the API installs its packages by
# name, and the services copy source directly.
/.python-version
/.pre-commit-config.yaml
/conftest.py
**/tests/
**/test_*.py
**/*.db
